<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohillas</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rohilla Afghans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rohillas were Pashtun (Afghan) soldiers and settlers who came to northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from the late 17th century and settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/katehr">Katehr</a> region, which became known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilkhand">Rohilkhand</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-mohammed-khan">Ali Mohammed Khan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafiz-rahmat-khan">Hafiz Rahmat Khan</a> they built a state in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rohilla-war">Rohilla War</a> of 1774 only their state of Rampur survived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rohillas.jpg" alt="Rohillas" width="320" height="517" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:North_Indian_Pastun_Recruit_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
